WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:05.970
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and during my
Game Of Thrones episode 7 video I asked you

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.670
all to submit questions so I picked 10 of
them to include in this video and one bonus

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.670
question.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:15.010
Also congratulations to Leslie Hernandez , you’re
this week’s giveaway winner.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.360
You win a $20 Amazon Giftcard.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.939
I’ll be messaging you on your channel for
details.

00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:20.410
If you’re just finding me for the first
time.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.810
I do Q&amp;As like this for most of my biggest
stuff like Game of Thrones or if there’s

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.070
something special you guys want to talk more
about.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.689
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
feel free to leave me suggestions for bonus

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:33.689
videos.

00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:35.972
After the Q&amp;A I’ll have an update on my
schedule this week.

00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:38.630
It’s going to be a little weird, but there’s
some cool stuff coming.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.810
So let’s answers some Moon Door Questions,
careful for spoilers from the episode if you

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:42.810
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:47.860
Here we go Question 1 - Sarah asks What do
you think Melisandre will do with Stannis'

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:48.860
daughter?

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.040
I don’t remember that from the books.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.360
I think Melisandre is going to try and sacrifice
her to gain some boon from the Red God.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.720
It seems like her using Royal Blood makes
her spells much more powerful.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.660
Like when she used Stannis to make the shadow
baby, she probably couldn’t have done that

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.500
with any normal person.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.970
It had to be someone with Royal Blood.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:11.820
The show doesn’t really explain why, only
that Royal Blood is special in the eyes of

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.820
the Red God.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.490
It’s a lot like the way a Cleric prays to
a God for their powers and the god grants

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.500
them power for a short period of time.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.280
That’s they way I view Melisandre and Thoros’
abilities.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:30.690
It’s not like sorcery where you get your
powers from a mystical place.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.210
As for what she’s hoping to get from Shireen’s
royal blood I can’t say.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.490
I think it’s just to make their army stronger.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.490
To assure victory.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.890
Question 2 - Pizza Dalek says I think Littlefinger
kissed Sansa because he knew Lysa was watching

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.180
and it was all part of a big scheme.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.920
He kissed her for a bunch of reasons.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.120
Part because he was working a long con to
get rid of Lysa, she was just a means to an

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.450
end.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.330
But he also has really conflicted feelings
about Sansa.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.850
He said it all in his speech there.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.150
She is for him several things, the daughter
he never had.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.909
And a much more beautiful version of the only
woman he ever loved.

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:12.590
So he’s part sentimental, part creeper.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.710
As for how Sansa feels about all this, I’d
say she’s just shocked and doesn’t know

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:17.710
what’s going on.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:22.720
Remember, she’s learning to be a pessimist
but she still has a lot of that innocence

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.720
left in her.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.690
So she’s not even thinking about Littlefinger
trying to get rid of Lysa.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.340
Question 3 - Kirsten Knightley asks why did
Daenerys let the Masters keep their power

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.630
and wealth?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.650
They made it seem like she crucified those
few hundred arbitrarily, like she didn’t

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:37.650
give them a trial.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.960
She just said you hung up X number of slaves
so I’m going to hang up X number of slave

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:42.960
masters.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.870
I think the show is going to explain a little
more about her relationship with the rest

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.790
of the slaving families in Meereen.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.850
She’s the current power in the city, so
a lot of them are just sucking up to her like

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.120
sycophants in King’s Landing do with the
Iron Throne.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.040
She really did kill a lot of them though.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.099
But all of the slaving families have sons
like Hizdhar, so killing the fathers just

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:02.900
means the sons will take over.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:07.870
So if she really wanted to get rid of slaving
completely, she’d have to kill all of the

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:08.890
families.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:12.330
Which is way way more people and as much of
a badass as she is, I don’t think she’s

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.879
prepared to murder that many people.

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:20.660
She is giving them the chance to accept her
rule.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:24.660
Question 4 - Relle Laron asks Do you think
we’ll see Gendry this season?

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:32.069
I hope so, there was a tweet that Joe Dempsie
wrote saying he worked with a bunch of awesome

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:35.250
people this year and one of them was Maisie
Williams.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.450
I think it’s okay to assume he was talking
about Game of Thrones because the only other

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.650
project on her IMDB page doesn’t list Joe
Dempsie as a cast member.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.849
It’s more likely that he just has a greatly
reduced role.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:50.590
Remember, the last time we saw him, he was
rowing for King’s Landing from Dragonstone.

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.659
So it’s possible he could have been picked
up by a ship or he really will make it back

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:55.980
to King’s Landing.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:01.150
They’ve already changed his character from
the books a lot, so I don’t want to try

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:04.030
and predict too many things about him.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.190
Question 5 - Bloody Desires asks Did Brienne
choose to follow Pod's suggestion about Sansa

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.350
being with her aunt?

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.472
Yes, it was really subtle, but they are heading
for the Vale.

00:04:13.472 --> 00:04:14.600
It’s possible that they could catch up to
Arya and the Hound.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.590
I don’t think it will be as simple as them
just finding Sansa at the Vale.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.530
That seems too nice of an ending for Game
of Thrones.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.919
So I’m planning on something terrible happening
on their journey.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:27.330
Either they run into the Brotherhood and someone
dies, or they run into Arya and the Hound

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.330
and someone dies.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.599
Someone is probably going to die.

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:35.760
Question 6 - Declan Asks could you explain
who Lolly’s Stokeworth is?

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.340
I saw a bunch of people in the comments asking
about Lollys.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.532
She’s a minor character from King’s Landing
in the books.

00:04:44.532 --> 00:04:48.520
In season 2 when all the peasants rioted and
tried to kill Joffrey, in the books.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.630
Her character is brutalized by the mob.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:55.110
She’s from a noble house, but after the
mob attack, no one is willing to marry her.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:05:02.250
But Bronn comes along and Cersei tries to
win him over, to turn against Tyrion by offering

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.870
him a title and a castle and marriage to Lollys.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:10.680
So Bronn is marrying into money, and as you
can see, he’s not too picky about his women.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:16.340
They cut her character out of the show is
all.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.750
Until now.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.220
Question 7 - Nicholas asks What was the Mountain
doing with all those guys?

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.979
He was executing them for petty crimes.

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:27.169
Like normally you would just lock people up.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:29.880
The Mountain was just slaughtering them like
Cattle.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.230
The reason it’s so terrible is because they
all probably just committed minor crimes.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.389
The Mountain is like a crazier version of
ser Illyn Payne.

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:39.360
Payne is the King’s executioner.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.830
But he has scruples.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.790
The Mountain is who you call when you want
someone killed, no questions asked.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.830
He’s like a fixer for the Lannisters.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:47.830
Fixing inconvenient problems.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:54.350
They showed that scene just to let us know
how crazy dangerous he is.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:58.680
Question 8 - Nathan asks Why do Lysa and her
son seem to have years of inbreeding in their

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.669
blood?

00:06:01.669 --> 00:06:05.039
All royals have a certain level of interbreeding
going on.

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:10.669
Like there aren’t that many people to pick
from to marry from other families over the

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:16.810
course of the centuries without you ending
up being related to everyone else at some

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.810
point.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.540
But Lysa is a Stark, so she’s not born of
incest or anything.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.880
And she wasn’t related to John Arryn when
they were married.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.330
So technically Robyn isn’t a twincest baby
like Joffrey.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.360
He’s just super nutters.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.332
In the books, Tyrion describes Lysa as being
‘touched’ as in she’s crazy.

00:06:32.332 --> 00:06:33.730
Just mentally disturbed.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:38.160
That’s why Littlefinger has had such an
easy time of manipulating her over the years.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:44.450
Although he probably contributed to some of
her psychosis.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:49.800
Question 9 - Ashley asks, could you explain
Oberyn’s speech about baby Tyrion more?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.490
So Tyrion is several years younger than Oberyn,
Jaime and Cersei.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:59.199
So when he was born at Casterly Rock it just
happend to coincide with a vist from the Martells.

00:06:59.199 --> 00:07:00.199
Oberyn would have been a little boy.

00:07:00.199 --> 00:07:02.789
They were just visiting the Lannisters.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:05.690
But while they were on their way, Tyrion was
born and his mother died.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:10.260
So everyone at Casterly Rock including Cersei
started telling stories about Tyrion being

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.100
a monster and killing their mother.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:17.009
They don’t explain Cersei’s thought process
a lot, other than she decides to put all of

00:07:17.009 --> 00:07:19.890
her negative feelings for her mother dying
on Tyrion.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.020
She just blames him.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.500
Jaime does not.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:27.270
So Oberyn goes to see Tyrion in his cradle
and just like Jaime, decides that Tyrion isn’t

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.210
a monster at all, he’s just a little baby.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:32.919
They’re just trying to show that Oberyn
has a lot of compassion.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.020
As opposed to Cersei.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:38.840
Question 10 - Nick asks Do you think Bran
would ever be able to warg into one of Daenerys’

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:39.840
dragons?

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.282
They don’t explain the science of it too
well, but it’s implied that a lot of it

00:07:44.282 --> 00:07:47.410
has to do with the mental strength of the
vessel.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:52.050
So it would be a lot harder for Bran to Warg
into a person of normal intelligence.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.759
As opposed to Hodor whole has a much more
primitive brain.

00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:58.350
It depends on how smart the Dragons are.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.850
They seem like they’re a lot more powerful
than the direwolves.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.280
So I think Bran would have to be a lot better
at it.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:13.300
Like becoming a more powerful Jedi before
you can take down Vader and the Emperor.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:18.580
Bonus Question - Bombay Theme asks, What did
Daenerys mean when she told Jorah to tell

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.850
Daario he changed her mind?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:27.199
She was originally going to have Daario execute
all the Wise Masters in Yunkai but Jorah reasoned

00:08:27.199 --> 00:08:33.610
that her new followers would just see it as
more brutality and revolt against her.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:38.339
So his idea was to at least give them the
choice to accept Daenerys’ terms.

00:08:38.339 --> 00:08:43.519
Daenerys was just throwing him a bone by telling
him to tell Daario that he changed her mind.

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:47.480
I think she feels a little guilty about favoring
Daario now.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:51.639
When Jorah has been loyal to her for so long.

00:08:51.639 --> 00:08:55.639
She she’s just showing him that she hasn’t
forgotten about him completely.

00:08:55.639 --> 00:08:58.209
So thanks so much everyone for submitting
questions.

00:08:58.209 --> 00:09:00.810
Remember, there’s no new episode for two
weeks.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.259
So this weekend I’ll just do a bonus video
instead.

00:09:03.259 --> 00:09:04.679
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:04.679 --> 00:09:06.879
And if you guys want I’ll do another Q&amp;A
too.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:07.879
Just let me know.

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:12.270
I’ll be traveling from Thursday through
Sunday, so there will probably only be one

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:16.420
video each day for those days but I’ll try
to post updates on my schedule on social.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:19.319
Links for all that in the description.

00:09:19.319 --> 00:09:24.459
Right now click here for my episode 7 video
and click here to learn all about the Wildlings.

00:09:24.459 --> 00:09:26.149
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:26.639
High Fives!

